# Root .gitignore
# Nested .gitignore files in backend/ and desktop/ handle their own tooling.
# This file covers repository-wide concerns.

# --- Accounting data: must never be committed ---
# This repository builds a financial application. A .db file is a real
# business database containing the user's financial records. Committing one
# leaks customer data, supplier data, and money figures into version history,
# where deleting it later does not remove it.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
accounting-FY-*.db
# Desktop backup snapshots produced by backup/restore
*.db.bak
*.db.backup
/backups/
/desktop/backups/

# --- Licence and secret material ---
# The backend private signing key must never enter version control.
*.pem
*.key
!backend/storage/*.key.example
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- OS and editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.db
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.idea
*.iml

# --- AI agent tooling state ---
# Local agent/worktree bookkeeping, not part of the project.
.kilo/

# --- Build output (belt and braces; desktop/.gitignore also covers /build/) ---
**/build/
**/node_modules/
*.log

# --- Local scratch ---
*.tmp
*.bak
scratch/
tmp/
